ixfelix-bot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/felixfelix-bot/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Thanks for the well-structured NIP-17 order chat read pipeline.\n\n1. **Good**: Input validation (pubkey format, limit bounds, timeout) happens before any signer or relay access — correct security boundary ordering.\n2. **Good**: Error mapping does not leak private relay payloads or internal failure messages — verified by tests checking `JSON.stringify(result)` does not contain private strings.\n3. **Good**: `Promise.all` with internal try-catch in `readLegacySafely`/`readNip17Safely` correctly implements degraded mode — both sources complete independently and the merge handles partial failure.\n4. **NIT**: `snapshotInput` has many defensive try-catch blocks around property access — verbose but correct for untrusted input. Could simplify with a safe-access helper if this pattern recurs.\n5. **Note**: This PR depends on #1136 — must not merge before it.\n6. **Good**: 1300+ lines of tests covering input boundary, relay-list discovery, targeting, message mapping, and correlation classification.\n7. **Good**: Deterministic representative selection for equivalent NIP-17 records (gift-wrap ID comparison) prevents wrapper identity from establishing false freshness.\n\nHappy to help with the integration cutover.","state":"COMMENTED","html_url":"https://github.com/PlebeianApp/mark